\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item Partial is often legitimate (a single-condition study has nothing to vary); the booleans say which check failed and the caller decides.
\item On the 1,236-file bigbio curated corpus at 4f823dcd mzLib measured 300 Informative, 742 Partial, 194 Skeleton.
\item Organism is excluded from sample_is_described because a search can fill it without a human describing the samples.
\item Looks only at the sample half; says nothing about structure (sdrf validate) or cross-file agreement (sdrf lint).
}
}
\section{Performance}{
Every call starts one bridge process, which costs a .NET start-up before any work. For many files call \code{\link{sdrf_assess_many}()} once rather than looping this function: one process, one start-up, and the thread count stated on the wire.
}
